{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When there is a dispute.</b> Its end is that they come to judgment. Say henceforth: no peace comes out of a quarrel. Who caused Lot to separate from the righteous one? Say: this — quarrel." "<b>And they condemn the guilty.</b> One might think all who are liable in court receive lashes — Scripture says: <b>And it shall be, if the guilty one is to be lashed.</b> Sometimes he is lashed and sometimes he is not lashed. And who is the one lashed? Learn from the context: ״לֹא תַחְסֹם שׁוֹר בְּדִישׁוֹ״ — a prohibition not attached to a positive command (see Sifrei; Makkot 13)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:17.889465461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}